+///
+/// GODOT WEBGPU PATCH: was SPV_ENV_VULKAN_1_1 (SPIR-V <=1.3) upstream, which
+/// rejects any SPIR-V 1.4 input outright: "Invalid SPIR-V binary version 1.4
+/// for target environment SPIR-V 1.3 (under Vulkan 1.1 semantics)". Godot's
+/// WebGPU driver deliberately targets SPIR-V 1.3 (see
+/// drivers/webgpu/rendering_shader_container_webgpu.h), so this fork's real
+/// pipeline never actually emits 1.4 -- this was found chasing a red herring
+/// (GODOT_DUMP_SPIRV captured via `--rendering-driver vulkan`, whose container
+/// deliberately requests 1.4, unlike WebGPU's 1.3; see webgpu_notes/TASKS.md
+/// Task 8.6 for the full diagnosis writeup). Bumped anyway, and kept, as cheap
+/// defense-in-depth: SPV_ENV_VULKAN_1_2 (SPIR-V <=1.5) covers 1.4 with margin,
+/// in case a future SPIR-V version bump or some other 1.4 input ever reaches
+/// this reader. See thirdparty/README.md's `## tint` patch list.
+constexpr auto kTargetEnv = SPV_ENV_VULKAN_1_2;
 
